{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 2 of the 1966 FIFA World Cup''' consisted of [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]], [[Germany national football team|West Germany]], [[Spain national football team|Spain]], and [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]]. Play began on 12 July 1966 and concluded on 20 July 1966. West Germany won the group and Argentina finished as runners-up, and both advanced to the quarter-finals. Spain and Switzerland failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stokkermans |first1=Karel |last2=Jarreta |first2=Sergio Henrique |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/66f.html |title=World Cup 1966 (England, July 11–30) |website=RSSSF.com |publisher=[[Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation]] |date=22 October 1999 |access-date=26 May 2018}}</ref>

